# Patterns are deliberately depth-independent (`**/dist/` rather than `dist`).
#
# Prettier resolves an ignore file's patterns relative to that file's own directory, so a
# bare `dist` here only ever meant `<repo root>/dist` — it did not match apps/desktop/dist,
# apps/server/dist, or any of the package builds. Each workspace's `format` script runs
# prettier from inside that workspace, which made this worse: prettier only auto-loads a
# `.prettierignore` from its working directory, so this file was not read at all and
# compiled output got rewritten. Those scripts now pass `--ignore-path` explicitly, and
# these patterns match wherever they are resolved from.
#
# node_modules is not listed: prettier skips it unless `--with-node-modules` is passed.

# Build output
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.next/
**/out/
**/.output/
**/.vinxi/

# Test and tooling output
**/coverage/

# Lockfiles — machine-written, and reformatting one produces a huge meaningless diff
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
yarn.lock
bun.lock

# Generated sources
**/routeTree.gen.ts
**/next-env.d.ts

# Captured upstream responses used as scraper test fixtures. Real sites emit malformed
# markup — prettier refuses to parse some of these outright — and the point of a fixture
# is that it is byte-for-byte what the source actually served. Reformatting one changes
# the thing under test.
**/__tests__/fixtures/

# Project guidance and plans. These are hand-authored prose,
# and prettier's markdown rules rewrite tables, list markers and line wrapping in ways
# that produce large diffs for no gain. The generated framework guidance is rewritten
# by `next dev`, so formatting it just gets undone on the next run.
.claude/
**/CLAUDE.md
**/AGENTS.md
